  "body": "Stacked on #1817 (merge #1817 first)\n\n## What changed\n- Added `crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest_rings.rs` (`rest_passes`, `clip_loop`, `chain_pieces`) to clip `plan.center` waterline offsets against `cut_zone = plan.rest.offset(r + REST_REACH * 0.5)` (`r + 0.025` mm) and chain surviving pieces interior-out within `cut_center = cut_zone.intersect(&plan.center)`.\n- Added `crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest_anchor.rs` (`anchor_first_pass`) to re-anchor a pinched-tip open first pass into nearby dive room of its connected component (walking to the tip and doubling back) and rotate a closed first pass toward dive room when its seam lacks clearance.\n- Extracted pocket pass emission from `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket.rs` (`pocket_over`) into `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_emit.rs` (`emit_pocket_passes`, `PocketWalks`) so `rest_pocket` keeps identical arc fitting, corner blending, crossing guards, and level links while bounding `links_center` to `&cut_center`.\n- Updated `crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs`, `crates/app/tests/golden/pocket_rest_corners.cl`, and `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs` with strict cleared-floor feed pins, and documented choices in `docs/decisions/1816-rest-corner-air.md`.\n\n## Cause\n`rest_pocket` previously handed `plan.center` (`rest.offset(r + 0.05).intersect(own_center)`) directly to `pocket_over`'s waterline generator. Each closed offset loop of a crescent rest region fed along the crescent's inner boundary `r + 0.05` mm away from rest stock over already-cleared floor (and closed hole loops under large `previous_stock_to_leave` walked pure air), while opening a ring left pinched corner tips where `descent::plan` fed across cleared floor from the interior to the tip.\n\n## Tests\n- **Pins (all failed on `base-1817` before fix, pass after fix):**\n  - `crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs::read_against_the_simulated_roughing_pass` (tightened `r.2 < 0.5`; previously ~6.72 mm cleared-floor feed per ring across 8 corner runs) — `app rest_pocket` 6/6 ok.\n  - `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs::rest_rings_do_not_feed_over_cleared_floor` (failed at `55.38 mm` cleared-floor feed; covers `Waterline`, `OffsetRings`, `Auto` x `climb` x `Plunge`/`Helix`/`Ramp`) — ok.\n  - `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs::deep_corner_and_filleted_turns_clear_residue_without_cleared_floor_laps` (failed at `79.95 mm`; covers `blend_turns`, `Links::PLANAR`/`Links::ROUGH3D`, deep crescents) — ok.\n  - `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs::previous_stock_to_leave_drops_cleared_floor_hole_lap` (failed at `348.68 mm`; covers `leave=0.3` and `leave=5.8` inner hole-lap dropping/keeping) — ok.\n- **Mutations:**\n  - Restored `base-1817:crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest2d.rs`: all three `rest2d` pins and `read_against_the_simulated_roughing_pass` FAILED -> restored -> PASSED (`rest2d` 13/13, `rest_pocket` 6/6).\n  - Disabled `anchor_first_pass` in `rest2d.rs`: `rest_rings_do_not_feed_over_cleared_floor` FAILED (`0.79 mm` cleared-floor feed) -> restored -> PASSED.\n  - Changed `cut_zone` margin in `rest_rings.rs` from `r + REST_REACH * 0.5` to `r + REST_REACH`: `rest_rings_do_not_feed_over_cleared_floor` FAILED -> restored -> PASSED.\n- **Gate & Clippy (after final code edit):**\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: 0 warnings, exit 0.\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` across all 3 planned steps (`--only ui`: ok 302s; `--only motion`: ok 1460s; `--only app`: ok 2967s; 0 failed). Steps ran individually so `app suites` (49.5 min alone) stayed under the session runner window.\n\n## Goldens moved\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/pocket_rest_corners.cl` (added by #1817; vs `base-1817`: `moves=126` -> `moves=84`, 42 moves removed across 3 Z levels `20000`/`18000`/`16000`). Each of the 4 corners drops its cleared-floor inner return arcs (`Arc`/`Feed`), and Corner 1 re-anchors from `(27625, 17307)` to `(27700, 16451)` to cut the tip wall before sweeping the corner arc.\n\n## Not exercised\n- `cargo xtask gate release` (heavy `--ignored` suites and UI pixel snapshots).\n- Rest pocket interactions with horizontal `arc_xy` or predrilled-hole reseating, and neck/island rest geometries beyond rounded rectangular pockets.\n\n## Overlaps\n- **Stacked on #1817** (merge #1817 first; touches `rest2d.rs`, `machining2d/mod.rs`, `tests/rest2d.rs`, `crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs`, `crates/app/tests/golden/pocket_rest_corners.cl`).\n- **Same files, different scope (whichever merges second refreshes):**\n  - `#2129` edits `pocket_over`'s `.with_top(p.top_z)` line in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket.rs` (extracted into `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_emit.rs` here).\n  - `#2149` changes visibility of `PocketParams::validate` / `tiling_step` in `pocket.rs` and edits `machining2d/mod.rs`.\n  - `#2037` edits `rest_strategy` and `Zigzag` rest paths/tests in `rest2d.rs`, `pocket.rs`, `machining2d/mod.rs`, `tests/rest2d.rs`, `tests/rest_pocket.rs`, `pocket_rest_corners.cl`.\n  - `#2093` edits UI rest group, `machining2d/mod.rs`, `rest2d.rs`, and the rest-pocket tests/golden.\n  - `#2035` edits the `Adaptive` arm of `pocket_over` in `pocket.rs` and `machining2d/mod.rs`.\n  - `#2114` and `#2116` add modules in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs`.\n\nChangelog: Fix 2D pocket rest machining feeding across cleared floor on inner corner ring legs\nFixes #1816\n\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Pocket page before/after\n\nThe Pocket Passes page is unchanged visually. These real egui_kittest renders use the same existing fixture at 720×900. Before uses the upstream/main `dab6498a` page implementation, with only a `..` compatibility wildcard to ignore the new rest field against the PR struct. After uses unchanged PR head `0b0872d18`. The images are byte identical, as expected. The capture source was restored.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Pocket Passes page before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4d6408a5eb318eafa833785f0262d2d3b1d155ed/2154/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Pocket Passes page after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/4d6408a5eb318eafa833785f0262d2d3b1d155ed/2154/after.png)\n",
